    "recommendations": "• Thin trees within the cluster nearest to the structure to create more open space between individual trees.\n• Trim lower branches on large trees close to the structure to raise the canopy off the ground.\n• Cut back shrubs that are directly touching or within a few feet of the structure's walls or foundation.\n• Mow or cut grass cover close to the structure, particularly where it grows up against the building.\n• Keep grass in open areas around the structure cut short during dry periods.\n• Remove dead or dry grass accumulation from beneath scattered shrubs near the structure.\n• Trim overhanging branches from large trees above the roofline or gutters.\n• Keep both access routes clear of low-hanging branches and encroaching vegetation along the edges.\n• Maintain open ground between the scattered trees and any outbuildings or fencing connected to the main structure.\n• Remove any dead branches or debris that has accumulated under the tree cluster closest to the structure."
